{{!
    @template aiprovider_datacurso/plugin_list_page

    Table of the Datacurso suite plugins in the plugins tab of the provider reports: name, description,
    whether the plugin is installed, a switch that enables or disables it in the provider (installed
    plugins only), a link to its settings page in the provider (only when the plugin adds its own fields)
    and an icon link to its page on moodle.org. The switch follows the core AI "Actions" tables.

    Classes required for JS:
    * none

    Data attributes required for JS:
    * data-region="aiprovider_datacurso/plugin_list" - Root of the table.
    * data-action="aiprovider_datacurso/plugin_list/toggle-enabled" - Switch of one plugin.
    * data-component - Component the switch belongs to.
    * data-name - Display name of the plugin, for the "Enable X" / "Disable X" label.
    * data-state - Current state of the switch, 1 or 0.
    * data-tenantid - Scope the switch changes: a tenant id, or 0 for the site default. Absent for the tenant
      of the current user.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * hasplugins bool - True when there is at least one plugin to list.
    * scopenotice string - Which scope the switches change (Moodle Workplace); empty for none.
    * scopeselector string - Rendered selector of the scope for site administrators; empty for none.
    * plugins array - One entry per suite plugin, each with:
        * component string - Frankenstyle component name.
        * name string - Display name of the plugin.
        * description string - Short description of the plugin.
        * url string - Page of the plugin on moodle.org.
        * linktitle string - Accessible name of the moodle.org link.
        * installed bool - Whether the plugin is installed on this site.
        * enabled bool - Whether the plugin is enabled in the provider.
        * hastoggle bool - Whether to show the switch (installed plugins, for users who may manage them).
        * toggle object - Context of the core/toggle switch; present when hastoggle is true.
        * hassettings bool - Whether to show the settings link (only plugins with their own fields).
        * settingsurl string - Settings page of the plugin in the provider; empty when hassettings is false.

    Example context (json):
    {
        "hasplugins": true,
        "scopenotice": "These switches apply only to your tenant.",
        "scopeselector": "",
        "plugins": [
            {
                "component": "local_jedomi",
                "name": "Jedomi",
                "description": "AI assistant for Moodle users with chat, tools and scheduled agents.",
                "url": "https://moodle.org/plugins/local_jedomi",
                "linktitle": "Jedomi link",
                "installed": true,
                "enabled": true,
                "hastoggle": true,
                "toggle": {
                    "id": "aiprovider_datacurso-plugin-toggle-local_jedomi",
                    "checked": true,
                    "dataattributes": [
                        {
                            "name": "action",
                            "value": "aiprovider_datacurso/plugin_list/toggle-enabled"
                        },
                        {
                            "name": "component",
                            "value": "local_jedomi"
                        },
                        {
                            "name": "name",
                            "value": "Jedomi"
                        },
                        {
                            "name": "state",
                            "value": 1
                        }
                    ],
                    "title": "Disable Jedomi",
                    "label": "Disable Jedomi",
                    "labelclasses": "sr-only"
                },
                "hassettings": true,
                "settingsurl": "https://example.com/ai/provider/datacurso/admin/plugin_settings.php?component=local_jedomi"
            },
            {
                "component": "report_lifestory",
                "name": "Student Life Story AI",
                "description": "AI-powered report and analysis of the student's academic progress.",
                "url": "https://moodle.org/plugins/report_lifestory",
                "linktitle": "Student Life Story AI link",
                "installed": false,
                "enabled": true,
                "hastoggle": false,
                "hassettings": false,
                "settingsurl": ""
            }
        ]
    }
}}
<div class="aiprovider_datacurso-plugin_list_page" data-region="aiprovider_datacurso/plugin_list">
    <p>{{#str}}descriptionpagelistplugins, aiprovider_datacurso{{/str}}</p>
    {{#scopeselector}}<div class="mb-3">{{{scopeselector}}}</div>{{/scopeselector}}
    {{#scopenotice}}<div class="alert alert-info" role="status">{{scopenotice}}</div>{{/scopenotice}}

    <table class="generaltable">
        <thead>
            <tr>
                <th scope="col">{{#str}}plugin, aiprovider_datacurso{{/str}}</th>
                <th scope="col">{{#str}}description, aiprovider_datacurso{{/str}}</th>
                <th scope="col">{{#str}}installed, aiprovider_datacurso{{/str}}</th>
                <th scope="col">{{#str}}pluginenabled, core_plugin{{/str}}</th>
                <th scope="col">{{#str}}pluginsettings, aiprovider_datacurso{{/str}}</th>
                <th scope="col">{{#str}}link_plugin, aiprovider_datacurso{{/str}}</th>
            </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
            {{#hasplugins}}
            {{#plugins}}
            <tr data-component="{{component}}"{{^enabled}} class="dimmed_text"{{/enabled}}>
                <td>{{name}}</td>
                <td>{{description}}</td>
                <td>{{#installed}}{{#str}}yes, core{{/str}}{{/installed}}{{^installed}}{{#str}}no, core{{/str}}{{/installed}}</td>
                <td>
                    {{#hastoggle}}{{#toggle}}{{> core/toggle }}{{/toggle}}{{/hastoggle}}
                    {{^hastoggle}}-{{/hastoggle}}
                </td>
                <td>
                    {{#hassettings}}<a href="{{settingsurl}}">{{#str}}pluginsettings, aiprovider_datacurso{{/str}}</a>{{/hassettings}}
                    {{^hassettings}}-{{/hassettings}}
                </td>
                <td>
                    <a href="{{url}}" target="_blank" rel="noopener" title="{{linktitle}}" aria-label="{{linktitle}}">
                        {{#pix}}i/externallink, core{{/pix}}
                    </a>
                </td>
            </tr>
            {{/plugins}}
            {{/hasplugins}}
            {{^hasplugins}}
            <tr>
                <td colspan="6">{{#str}}message_no_there_plugins, aiprovider_datacurso{{/str}}</td>
            </tr>
            {{/hasplugins}}
        </tbody>
    </table>
</div>
{{#js}}
require(['aiprovider_datacurso/plugin_list'], function(PluginList) {
    PluginList.init();
});
{{/js}}
